### coding zenka improvements
- :template-name: prefix syntax — `:bug-fix: task text` sets task_type
  explicitly, matched against yaml/context-templates/ filenames
- read_file pagination UI — offset/length now line-based, txt_box ASCII
  progress bar + exact next-call instruction shown on truncation
- loop detector — similar_response_prefix pattern (4 rounds, 120-char prefix)
  catches model stuck retrying same truncated tool call
- timeout notification — txt_box framed message injected into model context
  on retry: "request timeout — your last tool call was not executed — retry
  or simplify". model self-corrects instead of repeating the same call.
- vram safety margin — now config-readable via coding.cfg.vram_safety_mb
  (default 1024). useful when VRAM is tight (e.g. 9086MB model, 9327MB free)

### kimi reconnect fix
- kimi.handler.approval_request: pre-acquisition approvals now queued as
  pending instead of dropped. on reconnect kimi.session.acquired resets to 0;
  approvals during history catchup were silently dropped causing hung tasks.
  fix: queue them — flushed by existing kimi.connect auto-approve logic once
  session is acquired. (Qwen diagnosed the race condition, we applied the fix)

